      "body": "Samsung Foundry Taps Taiwan Partner Faraday to Land 2nm Cloud AI Chip Deal\nSamsung Electronics' foundry division is set to manufacture a U.S. cloud company's artificial intelligence chip on its 2-nanometer process, with Taiwan-based ASIC design specialist Faraday acting as the intermediary, according to industry sources cited by Chosun Biz.\nFaraday disclosed the design win at an investor briefing on Oct. 27, saying it had secured a project for an American customer's cloud AI chip. The contract is the largest in Faraday's history, valued in the tens of millions of dollars, with initial revenue expected in the first half of 2027. Samsung will handle wafer production, while Faraday is also working with other partners including Taiwan's UMC.\nThe customer originally planned to use a 4nm node but shifted to Samsung's 2nm Gate-All-Around process after weighing performance, power efficiency and product lifespan. The chip is expected to incorporate 3D custom DRAM, which stacks memory vertically",
